<Base title="About — Sudhansh Peddabomma" description="About Sudhansh Peddabomma." active="about">
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero" style="padding-top: 60px;">
      <h1>Hey, I'm Sudhansh.</h1>
    </section>

    <section class="section prose" style="padding-top: 0;">
      <p>
        I love learning and wandering into new domains, and I enjoy connecting ideas across fields
        to solve hard problems. Most of my work has lived where research meets real-world use:
        3D reconstruction, generative AI, and statistical modeling.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today I'm a software engineer at <strong>Glean</strong>, where I work on the slides and
        videos that its AI creates for people.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before that, I did research. At UC San Diego I worked with Prof. Henrik Christensen on
        real-time dense 3D SLAM with NeRFs and Gaussian splatting for robot navigation, and on a
        scalable tabletop rearrangement planner (ICRA 2025). At IIT Bombay I worked with
        Prof. Ajit Rajwade on likelihood methods for compressed sensing under saturation noise,
        published in <em>Signal Processing</em>, and on correcting permutation errors in group
        testing (ICASSP 2025). At University College London I worked with Prof. Marta Betcke on
        stochastic primal-dual networks for 3D tomography.
      </p>
      <p>
        Along the way: computer vision intern at Duality AI (Gaussian-splat digital twins in
        Unreal Engine), Data &amp; Applied Scientist intern at Microsoft (email recommendations for
        Outlook), and software engineering intern at FinIQ (derivatives pricing).
      </p>
      <p>
        I studied Computer Science at IIT Bombay, graduating with honors and a minor in
        Entrepreneurship, and did my master's at UC San Diego. I'm passionate about entrepreneurship
        and collaboration. Hit me up to talk research, startup ideas, or even sitcoms!
      </p>
      <h2>Before college</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>All India Rank 178 in JEE Advanced 2019</li>
        <li>Gold medal in the Indian National Astronomy Olympiad 2019 (top 39 students)</li>
        <li>3rd rank in the AIMSCS Statistics Olympiad 2019, across India and Sri Lanka</li>
        <li>Among the top 300 selected for the Indian National Olympiads in Mathematics, Physics, and Chemistry, 2019</li>
        <li>KVPY Fellowship, 2017 and 2018</li>
      </ul>
